<h1>Unyap</h1>

<p><em>Impatience, now a browser extension.</em></p>

<p>You clicked for the answer, not for ten minutes of intro. Unyap is a Chrome extension for YouTube: it finds the part of a video that answers its title, and <strong>Unyap it</strong> jumps there. A strip over the progress bar marks filler, context and substance, and <strong>Next good part</strong> skips to the next useful bit. If the title is never answered, it tells you.</p>

<p><a href="https://chromewebstore.google.com/detail/unyap/jbmhegfmbdlkpiilfnjpmdkflfooobfe"><strong>Get Unyap on the Chrome Web Store</strong></a>. It’s free.</p>

<img src="/assets/images/unyap-on-youtube.jpg" alt="Unyap on a YouTube video: the Unyap it, Previous and Next good part buttons over the player, a strip above the progress bar coloured yellow for filler and green for the interesting parts, and the debug panel counting 20 judgments in 2 API requests." width="1400" height="890">

<p>It runs in your browser with your own OpenAI API key. It uses OpenAI’s Decisions API, which answers every question about a video in a single request, so OpenAI bills your key about $0.001 per new video, and nothing for one you already analyzed. Nothing is sent to me, and I store no data. Other AI providers are coming soon.</p>

<p>I built it at the DevDay Community Hackathon in Berlin, October 2026.</p>

